# Portfolio Bento UI

All sections are one shared bento system — never separate page layouts.

## Core model

- Eight persistent boxes (`A`–`H`) live in `BentoGrid.jsx` as the same DOM nodes for every section.
- Hero defines the initial set. Later sections only reshape, reposition, hide, or reveal those same boxes.
- Changing section must: (1) fade old content out, (2) morph box geometry via Framer `layout`, (3) fade new content in.
- `null` placement = hide that box for the section. Do not unmount the outer `Box` shell.

## Section flow

| From → To | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| Hero → About | Content fades; boxes reshape into about layout |
| About → Projects | Unused boxes hide; remaining reshape into project containers |
| Projects → Skills | Same morph / hide / reveal |
| Skills → Contact | Same morph / hide / reveal |

## Rules when editing

- ❌ Do not add a new section as a standalone page, route, or fresh grid of cards.
- ❌ Do not create one-off panels outside `Box` `A`–`H`.
- ❌ Do not swap section UIs with hard cuts (opacity-only page swaps without layout morph).
- ✅ Put section content in `sections/*Content.jsx` as named exports matching box IDs (`A`–`H`).
- ✅ Update `LAYOUTS` / `LAYOUTS_MOBILE` in `BentoGrid.jsx` for placement only.
- ✅ Prefer reusing a box that already exists in the previous section so the morph is visible.

## Motion

- Box morph and content fade use shared tokens in `motion.js`.
- Use **ease-in-out** tweens (not soft slow springs) for layout morph — consistent in and out.
- Keep morph duration snappy (~0.45–0.55s). Content crossfade slightly shorter.
- Projects may own its own inner slide intro, but outer boxes still morph from the shared set.
